  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Which of the following is/are aromatic alcohol?</p><p><img height=\"135\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/591a1fbb-2da1-4cab-ac36-9f85554972c2-image.png\" width=\"455\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "R5VPt",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>IV</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "89gRz",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mdL9z",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KmC3L",
      "text": "Only&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The&nbsp;aromatic alcohols&nbsp;are those compounds in which the hydroxyl group is not directly attached to the nucleus but is linked to a carbon atom situated in a side-chain.</p><p>The compound<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;and compound<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the phenols, these&nbsp;are&nbsp;not the&nbsp;aromatic alcohols as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>OH</mi></math>&nbsp;group is directly attached to benzene ring.</p><p>The compounds&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>III</mi></math>&nbsp;are benzyl alcohols and these are aromatic alcohols as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>OH</mi></math>&nbsp;group is attached to the carbon atom which itself attached to benzene ring.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
